Chromium's own browser, and the four things between it and this machine.

content_shell is the embedder the Chromium tree ships - the browser the
Chromium team runs their own tests against - and building it is a different
claim from building a program written here that links Chromium's libraries.
It starts the processes a browser is made of, through the code Chromium
starts them with.

A -k 0 build of //content/shell:content_shell failed in 53 places. All 53
were four things, and every one of them is a line this port has drawn
before.

CRASHPAD, WHICH IS LINUX'S KERNEL AND A SERVICE THAT IS NOT THERE

45 of the 53. features.h, sys/prctl.h, sys/ptrace.h, SYS_rt_tgsigqueueinfo,
SYS_gettid, setresuid, ELF32_ST_VISIBILITY - crashpad's Linux half.

args.gn already said use_crash_key_stubs = true for exactly this reason and
it did nothing here, because content_shell reaches crashpad by a different
route: `if (!is_fuchsia)` on its deps, and then

    data_deps += [ "//components/crash/core/app:chrome_crashpad_handler" ]

which is a DATA dependency. Nothing links it and ninja builds it anyway.
M159 found the Vulkan loader the same way and M162 wrote down the
instrument: gn path cannot see data dependencies without --with-data.

Fuchsia is the platform Chromium already had in this position - it is
use_crash_key_stubs' own default - and a platform in the Linux family with
none of Linux's kernel is in the same one. The condition is named once, in
content/shell/common/shell_switches.h, because the four sites that have to
agree about it are in three files and the link found the one that did not.

LIBPFM4, WHICH IS perf_event_open(2)

8 more. google_benchmark asks for hardware performance counters `if
(is_linux)`, reaching them through //base/test:test_support, which
content_shell_lib depends on through //ui/aura:test_support. It is
has_linux_kernel, and google_benchmark runs without the counters.

A SHARED LIBRARY IN A STATIC PROGRAM

base/test:test_support publishes libtest_trace_processor.so, and it is a
shared_library deliberately - the comment on it says why: two sqlite
implementations with the same symbols, hidden behind a library boundary. A
platform whose programs are statically linked has no boundary to hide them
behind, and ld.lld says "attempted static link of dynamic object".
has_symbol_interposition is the flag that already means this, in
BUILDCONFIG.gn's own words.

CALLERS LEFT BEHIND, THE FOURTH AND FIFTH TIME

M164 wrote the sentence and this milestone met it twice more, both in TEST
SUPPORT - which is code a browser drags in and nothing else here had:

  - net::MockNetworkChangeNotifier declares SetAddressMapOwnerLinux and an
    override of GetAddressMapOwnerInternal under `#if BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX)`,
    while the class it mocks gates both on HAS_LINUX_KERNEL as well. An
    override of a method that is not there is found by a COMPILE - of
    something that includes the mock, which is never the thing that was
    gated.
  - NetworkServiceTestHelper overrides GetAddressMapCacheLinux, whose mojom
    method is behind use_network_interface_change_listener - which M160's
    patch 0041 gates on has_linux_kernel.
  - content/test:test_support compiles sandbox_status_service.cc `if
    (is_linux || is_chromeos)`, and it reports what SandboxLinux did.
    Patch 0047 gated SandboxLinux. That one is found by a LINK, and then
    its own caller in shell_content_utility_client.cc by a second link.

And one header rather than a feature: gpu's test_shared_image_interface.cc
includes <linux/memfd.h> for MFD_CLOEXEC. This platform has memfd_create(2)
and declares it, with that constant, in <sys/mman.h> where the rest of the
mapping calls are - so what is gated is the header.

WHAT IS NOT HERE

No sandbox arrives with any of this. content_shell is built with the same
seccomp-less, namespace-less configuration every other program in this port
uses, and the binary is checked for it: no crashpad::, no pfm_.

